  "summary": {
    "headline": "The energy-sharing game is an asymmetric Prisoner's Dilemma: rational self-interest leads both shops to monopolize, producing the worst joint outcome.",
    "findings": [
      "The unique pure-strategy Nash equilibrium is (Monopolize, Monopolize), yielding 20,000 / 22,000 MMK — the lowest combined payoff.",
      "The cooperative outcome (60,000 / 70,000) is Pareto-optimal and strictly better for both, but is not individually rational in a single shot.",
      "Under uncertainty, Maximin and Minimax-Regret criteria favor cooperation, while Expected-Value, Laplace, and Hurwicz favor monopolizing.",
      "Nash Arbitration identifies (60,000 / 70,000) as the max-product allocation, giving both shops a 2x+ gain over the disagreement point.",
      "In repeated play, Tit-for-Tat and Grim Trigger sustain cooperation, achieving 3x the payoffs of Always Defect."
